<title>GERMANY: Isar-Amperwerke eyes higher 96/97 profits.</title>
<headline>Isar-Amperwerke eyes higher 96/97 profits.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>German utility Isar-Amperwerke AG said on Tuesday that it expects to report higher operating and overall profits in its current 1996/97 business year.</p>
<p>Chief executive Alfred Bayer said that both its operating profit, which reached 98.4 million marks last year, and its overall profit, which was 106.2 million marks in 1995/96, would rise at the same rate in the year to end of June 1997.</p>
<p>Speaking in a text prepared for Tuesday's annual meeting, Bayer said Isar-Amperwerke's financial profit in the current year would be at around the same level as last year's 127.4 million marks while electricity sales would grow by one percent.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
